{
  "name": "krita_layer_transform",
  "description": "Move a paint layer or group by whole pixels: a transform mask on top of its masks holds the move, and the layer's own pixels never change. The first translate adds the mask, then moves it (two undo steps); a later one moves the same mask (one); undo_steps says which, and krita_history_step moves them together. The whole canvas is checked against protection and a leak is undone. Refused for a protected layer, one holding one or one in a protected group, a transform mask no translate made, and under Krita's cumulative undo. A KRA keeps the move; an ORA drops it, so an ORA save is refused. Duplicate a layer before translating it: a translated layer is not copied.",
